        "Treat the source chart as a starting point. Check whether it refers to body measurements, finished-garment measurements, insole length or an unclear mixture. Note the unit and whether a tolerance is stated. Then compare only like with like: flat chest width to flat chest width, inseam to inseam, outsole to outsole when relevant. Do not convert one dimension into a universal fit claim. The purpose is to reduce uncertainty, not to promise that a number will feel identical on every body or product."
