        "Keep the reference in the spreadsheet as a private note rather than copying a generic recommendation into every product row. A buyer who wants an oversized hoodie may choose a different comparison than a buyer who wants a close fit. The note should say what it represents: preferred relaxed fit, fitted T-shirt, room for a mid-layer or everyday shoe. This turns a size choice into a documented preference rather than an assumption based on a familiar label from another brand or seller."
